my arsenal in case it develops into a more agent native mental model that I can understand and that works with my workflows. For example, if it had task awareness, with task-worker mapping, hierarchical agents, honoring worktrees within projects, and allowing one to switch between projects quickly like the tmux Session Picker, that would be great.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","I installed herdr a while back, used it heavily for a week, and haven't touched it sense, mostly because its conceptual model was rough."]],["2026-10-06%20Tue/","source-block-980","Yesterday, I noticed that something in my My/Dotfiles installed, with herdr, an AI/Agent/Hook that loads context on session load. That's pretty inefficient! That means that all my sessions - even those that don't begin in herdr - get that loaded in. I need to fix that.",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation"]],["2026-10-06%20Tue/","source-block-1266","Ghost Gardener please investigate this and file a github issue",["My Thoughts","Selective skill activation","Yesterday, I noticed that something in my My/Dotfiles installed, with herdr, an AI/Agent/Hook that loads context on session load. That's pretty inefficient! Tha"]]],"format_version":5}